// HOW THE ROSTER WAS PRODUCED, AND WHAT THAT METHOD CANNOT SEE. Naming the instrument rather than
// transcribing its output (DESIGN section 6) is not available here in its strong form, because the
// instrument is a source sweep and not an entry point -- so the method is stated in full instead,
// and the honest consequence is stated with it.
//
// THE METHOD. Every .dag file outside .git and target, with whole-line `//` annotations blanked and
// string literals masked so prose cannot match. First pass: every `fn NAME` declaration whose
// signature up to the opening brace carries a `uses IDENT:` clause -- 604 distinct names over 606
// declaration sites, out of 59,712 function declarations. Second pass: every balanced argument list
// and every balanced record literal, split at top-level commas over round, square and curly
// delimiters ONLY, with each part tested for a DIRECT call to one of those 604 names -- direct
// meaning not behind a `=>` and not inside an unclosed nested brace, so a call in a lambda body is
// excluded because a deferred occurrence is not a sibling demand. A part list with two or more such
// parts is a site.
//
// THE DELIMITER DETAIL IS NOT A DETAIL. An earlier cut of the same sweep counted `<` and `>` as
// depth and therefore mis-split every list containing a match arm, since `=>` decremented the
// depth; it reported eight sites, two of which were a single `release_host_effect_live(handle:,
// exit:)` call whose second argument is a block, split in the middle. Those two dissolved when the
// delimiter set was corrected, and four of the remaining six survive here. The defect is recorded
// because it is the shape a reader should assume is present until the instrument is the compiler.
//
// WHAT THE SWEEP CANNOT SEE, stated as bounds rather than as an apology, because each is a face of
// the class whose population is UNMEASURED and must not be read as zero: a sibling that reaches an
// effect through a call chain without declaring one itself, which is the whole population above the
// narrower wall; a method-call receiver; a call reached through a value bound elsewhere; and any
// site in a module the sweep's text pass reads but the compiler would refuse.
//
// ONE FACE WAS MEASURED AND IS GENUINELY EMPTY, and it is recorded here rather than omitted because
// an absence with no positive control is not evidence. INFIX CONNECTIVE OPERANDS: a third pass
// extracted the two immediate operands of every `&&` and `||` -- the left by walking back over a
// balanced parenthesised call term and any trailing field accesses, the right by matching a call
// term forward -- and found 9,705 sites where BOTH operands are direct calls, of which ZERO have
// even one operand calling a uses-declaring function. The 9,705 is the positive control: the
// extractor demonstrably fires on the condition being present, so the zero is a reading and not a
// silence. That face matters independently because .dag `&&` does not short-circuit, so an effect
// to the right of a false left still runs; it is empty today and nothing keeps it empty.
//
// THE UNIQUENESS CHECK THAT STANDS IN FOR RESOLUTION. Each of the 23 distinct callee names appearing
// in the roster was searched for every `fn` declaration of that name corpus-wide: each has EXACTLY
// ONE, and that one is uses-declaring. A text sweep cannot resolve a name to a declaration, so a
// homonym would have made the census unsound in the one direction that matters -- counting a site
// whose callee is a different, effect-free function of the same spelling. That check is the reason
// `callee_resolution_is_unambiguous` is a field rather than a sentence: a later row whose name is
// not unique must carry false and be dispositioned, not counted.

fn site_is_argument_list(s: SiblingEffectSite) -> Bool {
  match s.list_kind {
    ArgumentList => true
    RecordLiteralFields => false
    InfixConnectiveOperands => false
  }
}

fn site_is_record_literal(s: SiblingEffectSite) -> Bool {
  match s.list_kind {
    ArgumentList => false
    RecordLiteralFields => true
    InfixConnectiveOperands => false
  }
}

fn site_is_infix(s: SiblingEffectSite) -> Bool {
  match s.list_kind {
    ArgumentList => false
    RecordLiteralFields => false
    InfixConnectiveOperands => true
  }
}

fn site_order_observably_matters(s: SiblingEffectSite) -> Bool {
  match s.stake {
    OrderObservablyMatters { shared_subject: _ } => true
    OrderNotObservableAtTodaysArguments { why_disjoint_today: _ } => false
    PredicateFalsePositive { why_the_model_excludes_it: _ } => false
  }
}

fn site_is_false_positive(s: SiblingEffectSite) -> Bool {
  match s.stake {
    OrderObservablyMatters { shared_subject: _ } => false
    OrderNotObservableAtTodaysArguments { why_disjoint_today: _ } => false
    PredicateFalsePositive { why_the_model_excludes_it: _ } => true
  }
}

fn sibling_effect_site_count() -> Int {
  length(sibling_operand_effect_sites)
}

fn sibling_effect_argument_list_count() -> Int {
  length(filter(sibling_operand_effect_sites, s => site_is_argument_list(s: s)))
}

fn sibling_effect_record_literal_count() -> Int {
  length(filter(sibling_operand_effect_sites, s => site_is_record_literal(s: s)))
}

fn sibling_effect_infix_count() -> Int {
  length(filter(sibling_operand_effect_sites, s => site_is_infix(s: s)))
}

fn sibling_effect_order_matters_count() -> Int {
  length(filter(sibling_operand_effect_sites, s => site_order_observably_matters(s: s)))
}

fn sibling_effect_false_positive_count() -> Int {
  length(filter(sibling_operand_effect_sites, s => site_is_false_positive(s: s)))
}

// THE NUMBER THE WALL WOULD REFUSE, which is the whole point of the carrier: every rostered site is
// refused by the narrower wall, including the ones whose order is not observable at today's
// arguments, because the wall refuses an UNDECLARED order and not an observed race.
fn sibling_effect_sites_the_wall_would_refuse() -> Int {
  length(filter(sibling_operand_effect_sites, s => site_is_false_positive(s: s) == false))
}
